---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Privacy policy — Expressive Tea Software';
const description =
  'What expressive-tea.io collects: no cookies, no analytics, no third-party requests. Only the access logs our web server keeps to run and protect the site.';

// Kept as a date, not a string, so the machine-readable and the human-readable
// versions of "when this changed" cannot drift apart.
const effective = new Date('2026-08-19T00:00:00Z');
const effectiveLabel = effective.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap measure policy">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Effective <time datetime={effective.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}>{effectiveLabel}</time>.
        This page describes <strong>expressive-tea.io</strong> — this site and nothing else.
      </p>

      <p>
        Expressive Tea Software is an open-source project based in Mexico. We publish
        frameworks; we do not run a service, sell anything, or keep accounts. This page says
        exactly what happens when you load this site, and nothing that does not happen.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site collects: nothing</h2>
      <p>
        These pages are static files. They set no cookies, read and write nothing on your
        device, and run no analytics. Loading a page makes no request to any other company:
        the fonts are served from this domain rather than a font CDN, and there are no
        embedded scripts, trackers, pixels, widgets, or embedded media.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because nothing is stored on your device, there is nothing to consent to, which is why
        this site shows no cookie banner.
      </p>

      <h2>What our web server records</h2>
      <p>
        Like every web server, ours writes an access log for each request: your IP address, the
        date and time, the page requested, the referring page if your browser sends one, and
        your browser's user-agent string. An IP address can identify a person, so we treat
        these logs as personal data.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use them only to operate the site and to investigate abuse or faults — never to
        build a profile, and never to identify individual visitors. They are held on our
        hosting provider's servers, are not combined with anything else, and are not sold,
        rented, or shared. Under the GDPR our lawful basis is legitimate interest
        (Article 6(1)(f)): running a website securely is not possible without them.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        This page links to GitHub, npm, and our documentation subdomains. Your browser contacts
        them only if you click, and once you do you are on their site under their privacy
        policy, not ours.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you may request access to your personal data, its correction or
        erasure, restriction of or objection to its processing, and you may complain to your
        national supervisory authority. Under Mexico's LFPDPPP you hold the ARCO rights —
        acceso, rectificación, cancelación y oposición.
      </p>
      <p>
        In practice the only data we hold about a visitor is a log line. To ask about it, write
        to <a href="mailto:support@expressive-tea.io">support@expressive-tea.io</a> with enough
        detail to locate the entry — roughly when you visited, and from which IP address.
      </p>

      <h2>If this changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we ever add analytics, it will be a cookieless one that does not collect personal
        data, and this page will say so before it ships. Any change is reflected in the
        effective date at the top.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Expressive Tea Software ·
        <a href="mailto:support@expressive-tea.io">support@expressive-tea.io</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-top: 2.2em;
  }

  .policy p {
    color: var(--cool);
  }

  .policy .lede,
  .policy strong {
    color: var(--white);
  }
</style>
